<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 first-half GDP up 3.1 pct period/period.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 first-half GDP up 3.1 pct period/period.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gross domestic product (GDP) rose a real 3.1 percent in the first half of calendar 1996 from the previous half-year period, the government's Economic Planning Agency (EPA) announced on Friday.  </p>
<p>Percentage changes in expenditure for first half of calendar 1996 against the previous period:</p>
<p>    (Real data)	   Jan-June 1996    July-Dec 1995</p>
<p> GDP				  +3.1	     +1.5</p>
<p> GNP				  +3.1	     +1.8</p>
<p> Domestic Demand		  +3.9	     +2.3</p>
<p>   Private			  +3.0	     +1.8</p>
<p>    Personal outlays	    +2.1	     +1.8</p>
<p>    Housing			 +14.3	    -5.7</p>
<p>    Capital spending	    +3.0	     +3.2</p>
<p>    Inventory changes	   -0.9	     +80.2</p>
<p>   Public			   +7.8	     +4.8</p>
<p>    Government outlays	  +2.4	     -0.5</p>
<p>    Capital spending	    +12.6	    +11.2</p>
<p>    Inventory changes	   +504.0	   -72.5</p>
<p> External Demand		  -84.7	    -48.8</p>
<p>   Exports			  -0.7	     +1.1</p>
<p>   Imports			  +5.4	     +8.6</p>
<p>(Note: Due to rounding, figures may not tally. Also, figures smaller than two decimal places are not shown.)</p>
</text>
